00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Claudette Okafor-Example: Welcome. Today is open Q and A on contracts. Vince is joining for the second half.

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Claudette Okafor-Example: First, a change. Starting October 1, every buyer signs the brokerage's buyer agreement before the first showing. Not before the offer. Before the first showing.

3
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Agent (Noel Pretendini): Can I write in a clause that the seller pays for a home warranty?

4
00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Claudette Okafor-Example: A home warranty request goes in the offer on the standard form. Anything custom, any clause you'd write yourself, runs by Vince first.

5
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Agent (Noel Pretendini): What if the listing agent wants us to use their own addendum?

6
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Vince Fictionale: Send it to me before your buyer signs anything. I review every non-standard addendum.

7
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Agent (Indigo Madeupson): Do we still get the transaction coordinator on every deal?

8
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Claudette Okafor-Example: Yes. Every deal goes to the transaction coordinator within 24 hours of acceptance, same as always.

9
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Agent (Indigo Madeupson): And the pond rule, is it still 21 days?

10
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:20.000
